/* ===========================================================================
   Make / model / year index, harvested from the NHTSA vPIC database
   (vpic.nhtsa.dot.gov, GetModelsForMakeIdYear), model years 1981-2026.

   This is REAL reference data, unlike the key details in data.js: it says which
   vehicles exist and what years they ran, nothing about keys. The lookup lists
   the models it knows that no key record covers, and the add-vehicle form uses
   it to keep make and model spelling consistent.

   2,356 models across 103 makes, back to 1981.
   Shape: { Make: { Model: [firstYear, lastYear] } }

   Harvested by make ID and vehicle type, which matters twice over. The first
   pass asked by make NAME, and vPIC matches a name as a substring: "Geo"
   came back with Peugeot's 405 and 505, because PEU-GEO-T contains it, and
   Mini came back with Mack, Pete, KW and Brockway Mini Homes. Asking by ID is
   exact. Asking for car, truck and mpv -- and not motorcycle, bus, trailer or
   incomplete chassis -- leaves out the 53 bikes Honda sold in 2015 alongside
   its four cars, which a car catalogue has no use for and which made the
   coverage gap look several times worse than it is.

   1 entries were still a body-builder's company name rather than a
   model and were dropped by name.

   Regenerate by re-running the harvest; it is a plain public API, no key
   needed. Scion is absent because vPIC has no such make -- Toyota filed them.
   =========================================================================== */
